{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Our garners</b> — the corners of our houses are full." "<b>Bringing forth</b> — an allusion to servants." "<b>From kind to kind</b> — מין, as in the Targum: למינו לזנוהי. So too וזנים מרוקחים. And the meaning: kinds of wheat, rice, millet, and the like. Some say from the root מזון, and this commentator said that the word מפיקים there in <b>our garners</b> is a word whose meaning shifts according to the requirement of the context, without connection." "<b>Our sheep thousands</b> — they produce a thousand." "<b>Ten-thousands</b> — from the root רבבה, by supreme power. And the meaning: our sheep — those that were thousands, in them were ten-thousands."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 144, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:45.834006596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}